{
  "raw": {
    "https://svsu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Main-Campus/International-Partnership-Coordinator_JR-1334": {
      "title": "International Partnership Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nJob Title: International Partnership Coordinator Full or Part Time: Full time Hours: 40 Exempt: Yes Supervisory Org: International Programs (PM) Job Description: JOB SUMMARY: Reporting to the Director of the Office of International Programs (OIP), the International Partnership Coordinator is responsible for managing and developing sustainable international partnerships with international universities around the world and offers services to inbound F-1 and J-1 exchange students from partner institutions.   This is a 1-year temporary position with the potential for renewal contingent on available funding.   ESSENTIAL DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES: Maintain and develop international partnerships (e.g. 1+3, 2+2, exchange partners, sponsored programs) that align with the university’s strategic priorities in collaboration with the Director of International Programs. Foster strong relationships with partner institutions through regular communication and engagement. Manage the international partnership programs budget and agreements. Prepare reports on partnership activities and keep track of exchange balance. Assists with the coordination of the agenda and logistical arrangements (including visa application and travel reservations) for SVSU delegations traveling internationally. Planning and coordination of the agenda and logistical needs for delegations and visiting scholars from partner institutions and organizations. Manage the apartments for international visiting scholars. Facilitate and lead local cultural trips for international students and scholars. Offer personal services and advising to help international students and scholars adjust and gain a sense of belonging within the campus community. Assist exchange students through application, enrollment, academic advising, cultural activities, credit transfer and billing. Track students, ratios, and budgets of student exchange programs. Facilitate cultural exchange events online with partnership program students in Asia and other international locations. Assist in hiring adjunct faculty to teach abroad at partner institutions. Manage the social media and create promotion materials for the partnership programs. Support the inbound Short-Study at SVSU programs of the partner schools. Translate partner school communications from English to Mandarin Chinese or vice versa as needed. Attend conferences for professional development. Perform other duties as assigned.   SUPERVISION RECEIVED: General supervision is received from the Director of the Office of International Programs.   SUPERVISION EXERCISED : Functional supervision is exercised over student assistants.   MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Master’s degree. Two/three years of professional experience. Must have a valid driver’s license. Ability to communicate effectively in Mandarin Chinese, both in spoken and written form. Must be able to travel both domestically and internationally, with a flexible schedule that accommodates travel. Must have excellent verbal and written communication skills. Initiative, independence and leadership skills are essential. Must have experience making presentations to large groups. Proficient in Microsoft Office Suite and ability to learn new software quickly. Experience and ability to positively interact with a diverse campus community. Ability to perform the essential duties of the position with or without accommodations.   PREFERED QUALIFICATIONS: Master's degree in Asian Studies, international education, or related field. Experience living or studying abroad. Customer-service oriented attitude. Team player with strong performance record.   WORKING CONDITIONS: Some weeknights and weekends (e.g., due to different time zones), including intermittent travel, will be required. Duties are generally performed inside and not exposed to adverse conditions. All work associated with this role must be performed within the state of Michigan, except for university-related travel, which may include domestic and international travel.   Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and throughout their employment. The university does not provide employment visa sponsorship now or in the future for this job classification.  Since SVSU does not participate in E-Verify, candidates for employment are not eligible for STEM OPT extensions.   The above reflects the general details considered necessary to describe the essential functions of the job. It shall not be construed as an exhaustive statement of duties, responsibilities, or requirements that may be inherent in the job.  It is not intended to limit or in any way modify the right of any supervisor to assign, direct, and control the work of employees under his/her supervision.  The use of a particular expression or illustration describing duties shall not be held to exclude other duties not mentioned that are of similar kind or level of difficulty. About SVSU: Saginaw Valley State University is a comprehensive university with more than 100 programs of study for its roughly 7,000 students. Located on a suburban campus in Michigan’s Great Lakes Bay Region, SVSU is committed to a supportive and empowering environment for students, faculty and staff. SVSU has been named a “Great College to Work For” on nine separate occasions. SVSU emphasizes undergraduate teaching and learning, and community-based research. SVSU has twice earned the Community Engagement classification from the Carnegie Foundation for the Advancement of Teaching, a distinction achieved by only 7 percent of U.S. colleges and universities. By their senior year, 84 percent of students have engaged with community employers and agencies in internships, field placements or some other component of their academic preparation. SVSU is establishing itself as a leader in STEAM education for the Great Lakes Bay Region, partnering with businesses, foundations and school districts to improve students’ performance in math, science and the arts at the middle school, high school and university levels.  SVSU is constructing the first university research facility on Lake Huron to improve public health and the economy in the Saginaw Bay watershed.   More than 70 percent of SVSU freshmen live on campus in student housing that is rated No. 2 among all public universities in the U.S. SVSU fields 21 varsity sports at the NCAA Division II level. The average class size is 23 students. For more information, please visit our website, http://www.svsu.edu ."
    },
    "https://svsu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Main-Campus/Clinical-Professional--Simulation_JR-1353": {
      "title": "Clinical Professional, Simulation",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nPart time\n\nJob Title: Clinical Professional, Simulation Full or Part Time: Part time Hours: 29 Exempt: No Supervisory Org: Nursing - NU Lab (JM-CP) Job Description: JOB SUMMARY: The Clinical Professional, Simulation will assist in facilitating simulation experiences for nursing students. This part-time position plays a key role in supporting a dynamic and realistic learning environment where students can practice clinical decision-making, teamwork, and communication skills in a safe, simulated setting.    This position will involve working scheduled simulation days based on the N-level the Clinical Professional is assigned to. Workdays and hours may vary throughout the semester depending on the simulation schedule and program needs. Additional hours may be available throughout the semester and during the summer.   ESSENTIAL DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES: Facilitate and support nursing simulation sessions for nursing students, including setup, operation, and debriefing.  Prepare simulation equipment, manikins, and lab spaces prior to sessions and ensure proper cleanup afterward.  Operate and troubleshoot simulation technology.  Collaborate with faculty and simulation staff to deliver effective, evidence-based learning experiences.  Assist in guiding students through simulation scenarios, reinforcing critical thinking and clinical reasoning.  Participate in maintaining simulation supplies, equipment, and inventory.  Support ongoing quality improvement of simulation activities.  Perform other duties as assigned. SUPERVISION RECEIVED: General supervision is received from the Simulation Lab Coordinator.    MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Bachelor’s degree required (preferably in nursing); will consider a bachelor’s in a related or applicable field.  Strong technical aptitude with the ability to quickly learn new simulation and audiovisual technologies.  Excellent communication, teamwork, and interpersonal skills.  Ability to create a supportive and engaging learning environment.  Experience and ability to positively interact with all members of the campus community Ability to perform the essential duties of the position with or without accommodations. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) or related field.  Previous experience in nursing education, simulation facilitation, or clinical instruction.  Familiarity with simulation software and high-fidelity manikins.  WORKING CONDITIONS: Duties are generally performed inside and not exposed to adverse conditions. All work associated with this role must be performed within the state of Michigan.   Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and throughout their employment. The university does not provide employment visa sponsorship now or in the future for this job classification.  Since SVSU does not participate in E-Verify, candidates for employment are not eligible for STEM OPT extensions.   The above reflects the general details considered necessary to describe the essential functions of the job. It shall not be construed as an exhaustive statement of duties, responsibilities, or requirements that may be inherent in the job.  It is not intended to limit or in any way modify the right of any supervisor to assign, direct, and control the work of employees under his/her supervision.  The use of a particular expression or illustration describing duties shall not be held to exclude other duties not mentioned that are of similar kind or level of difficulty. About SVSU: Saginaw Valley State University is a comprehensive university with more than 100 programs of study for its roughly 7,000 students. Located on a suburban campus in Michigan’s Great Lakes Bay Region, SVSU is committed to a supportive and empowering environment for students, faculty and staff. SVSU has been named a “Great College to Work For” on nine separate occasions. SVSU emphasizes undergraduate teaching and learning, and community-based research. SVSU has twice earned the Community Engagement classification from the Carnegie Foundation for the Advancement of Teaching, a distinction achieved by only 7 percent of U.S. colleges and universities. By their senior year, 84 percent of students have engaged with community employers and agencies in internships, field placements or some other component of their academic preparation. SVSU is establishing itself as a leader in STEAM education for the Great Lakes Bay Region, partnering with businesses, foundations and school districts to improve students’ performance in math, science and the arts at the middle school, high school and university levels.  SVSU is constructing the first university research facility on Lake Huron to improve public health and the economy in the Saginaw Bay watershed.   More than 70 percent of SVSU freshmen live on campus in student housing that is rated No. 2 among all public universities in the U.S. SVSU fields 21 varsity sports at the NCAA Division II level. The average class size is 23 students. For more information, please visit our website, http://www.svsu.edu ."
    },
    "https://svsu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Main-Campus/Assistant-Professor-of-Mathematics_JR-1341": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Mathematics",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nJob Title: Assistant Professor of Mathematics Full or Part Time: Full time Hours: 40 Exempt: Yes Supervisory Org: Mathematical Sciences (PM) Job Description: JOB SUMMARY:  The Department of Mathematical Sciences at Saginaw Valley State University invites a diverse pool of applicants to fill a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Mathematical Sciences positions beginning Fall 2027. A successful candidate will teach a variety of courses for majors and non-majors. Participation in department, college, and university service, and the development of an active research program is expected. Involvement in undergraduate student research is encouraged. The Department of Mathematical Sciences offers majors in mathematics, applied mathematics and mathematics for teacher certification, and plays a critical role in supporting the university’s general education program. Department members are actively engaged in developing and implementing innovative teaching methodologies and are prominently involved in campus-wide initiatives. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Ph.D. or equivalent in mathematics, applied mathematics, statistics, or a related field is required by appointment or ABD status with a scheduled dissertation defense date. Ability to perform the essential duties of the position with or without accommodations. Experience and ability to positively interact with all members of the campus community Ability to perform the essential duties of the position with or without accommodations.   PREFERED QUALIFICATIONS: College-level teaching experience is preferred. WORKING CONDITIONS: Duties are generally performed inside and not exposed to adverse conditions. All work associated with this role must be performed within the state of Michigan.     The above reflects the general details considered necessary to describe the essential functions of the job. It shall not be construed as an exhaustive statement of duties, responsibilities, or requirements that may be inherent in the job.  It is not intended to limit or in any way modify the right of any supervisor to assign, direct, and control the work of employees under his/her supervision.  The use of a particular expression or illustration describing duties shall not be held to exclude other duties not mentioned that are of similar kind or level of difficulty.   Applicants must apply online at www.jobs.svsu.edu. Please include a cover letter, vita, contact information for three references, a photocopy of transcripts (an unoﬃcial copy is suﬃcient), and statements regarding research and teaching.   For questions, please contact William Vautaw, search chair, at wvautaw@svsu.edu About SVSU: Saginaw Valley State University is a comprehensive university with more than 100 programs of study for its roughly 7,000 students. Located on a suburban campus in Michigan’s Great Lakes Bay Region, SVSU is committed to a supportive and empowering environment for students, faculty and staff. SVSU has been named a “Great College to Work For” on nine separate occasions. SVSU emphasizes undergraduate teaching and learning, and community-based research. SVSU has twice earned the Community Engagement classification from the Carnegie Foundation for the Advancement of Teaching, a distinction achieved by only 7 percent of U.S. colleges and universities. By their senior year, 84 percent of students have engaged with community employers and agencies in internships, field placements or some other component of their academic preparation. SVSU is establishing itself as a leader in STEAM education for the Great Lakes Bay Region, partnering with businesses, foundations and school districts to improve students’ performance in math, science and the arts at the middle school, high school and university levels.  SVSU is constructing the first university research facility on Lake Huron to improve public health and the economy in the Saginaw Bay watershed.   More than 70 percent of SVSU freshmen live on campus in student housing that is rated No. 2 among all public universities in the U.S. SVSU fields 21 varsity sports at the NCAA Division II level. The average class size is 23 students. For more information, please visit our website, http://www.svsu.edu ."
