    "https://svsu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Main-Campus/Adjunct-Faculty--Accounting_JR-304-1": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Accounting",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-06-26\nPart time\n\nJob Title: Adjunct Faculty, Accounting Full or Part Time: Part time Hours: 9 Exempt: Yes Supervisory Org: Accounting, Law and Finance (JM-AJ) Job Description: JOB SUMMARY: The Saginaw Valley State University (SVSU) Department of Accounting, Law & Finance seeks an adjunct faculty position for Fall 2025 and Winter 2026 to teach one or more courses in Accounting.  Current needs are Financial Accounting and Managerial Accounting.  The ability to teach in person on campus is required.  When you apply, please indicate if you can teach during the day, at night, or both. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Master of Business Administration (MBA), Master of Accountancy, or Master of Taxation PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: College-level teaching experience preferred. REQUIRED DOCUMENTS AND MATERIALS: Curriculum vitae or resume that highlights education, work experience, and teaching experience. Transcripts from your master’s program. Scheduled weekly hours vary depending on class contract load. Adjunct Faculty are hired each semester on an as-needed basis. About SVSU: Saginaw Valley State University is a comprehensive university with more than 100 programs of study for its roughly 7,000 students. Located on a suburban campus in Michigan’s Great Lakes Bay Region, SVSU is committed to a supportive and empowering environment for students, faculty and staff. SVSU was recognized as a “Great College to Work For” for 9 consecutive years (2016-2024). SVSU emphasizes undergraduate teaching and learning, and community-based research. SVSU earned the Community Engagement classification from the Carnegie Foundation for the Advancement of Teaching, a distinction achieved by only 7 percent of U.S. colleges and universities. By their senior year, 84 percent of students have engaged with community employers and agencies in internships, field placements or some other component of their academic preparation. SVSU is establishing itself as a leader in STEAM education for the Great Lakes Bay Region, partnering with businesses, foundations and school districts to improve students’ performance in math, science and the arts at the middle school, high school and university levels.  SVSU is constructing the first university research facility on Lake Huron to improve public health and the economy in the Saginaw Bay watershed.   More than 70 percent of SVSU freshmen live on campus in student housing that has been rated No. 1 among public universities in the U.S. (2018-2025). SVSU fields 20 varsity sports at the NCAA Division II level. The average class size is 23 students. For more information, please visit our website ,  http://www.svsu.edu ."
    },
    "https://svsu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/External/job/Main-Campus/Adjunct-Faulty--Kinesiology_JR-267": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Kinesiology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-06-26\nPart time\n\nJob Title: Adjunct Faculty, Kinesiology Full or Part Time: Part time Hours: 29 Exempt: Yes Supervisory Org: Kinesiology (JM-AJ) (Lisa Krissoff Boehm Job Description: JOB SUMMARY: The Department of Kinesiology invites applications for adjunct faculty positions teaching courses in the undergraduate K-12, Health Education/Physical Education Teacher Education Program and Exercise Science and Rehabilitation Medicine.  Current course needs include School Health (K-12, Health Education/Physical Education Teacher Education) and Exercise Physiology Lab. Applicants should indicate their educational background and clinical expertise, as well as their availability and ability to teach online or in a hybrid format. Instructional, Temporary, Exempt, Contract Position MINIMUM QUALIFICAITONS:  Bachelor's degree in health education/teaching and experience teaching health education at the K-12 level OR Master's degree in exercise science or a similar degree with experience teaching exercise physiology lab About SVSU: Saginaw Valley State University is a comprehensive university with more than 100 programs of study for its roughly 7,000 students. Located on a suburban campus in Michigan’s Great Lakes Bay Region, SVSU is committed to a supportive and empowering environment for students, faculty and staff. SVSU was recognized as a “Great College to Work For” for 9 consecutive years (2016-2024). SVSU emphasizes undergraduate teaching and learning, and community-based research. SVSU earned the Community Engagement classification from the Carnegie Foundation for the Advancement of Teaching, a distinction achieved by only 7 percent of U.S. colleges and universities. By their senior year, 84 percent of students have engaged with community employers and agencies in internships, field placements or some other component of their academic preparation. SVSU is establishing itself as a leader in STEAM education for the Great Lakes Bay Region, partnering with businesses, foundations and school districts to improve students’ performance in math, science and the arts at the middle school, high school and university levels.  SVSU is constructing the first university research facility on Lake Huron to improve public health and the economy in the Saginaw Bay watershed.   More than 70 percent of SVSU freshmen live on campus in student housing that has been rated No. 1 among public universities in the U.S. (2018-2025). SVSU fields 20 varsity sports at the NCAA Division II level. The average class size is 23 students. For more information, please visit our website ,  http://www.svsu.edu ."
